	(text "Test points (pin map section 4 recommendation):\nTP1 = PA8 (MCO_1, clock bring-up probe), TP2 = PB2,\nTP3 = PB4 (NJTRST at reset), TP4 = PD2 (only GPIOD pin)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250 180 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0b84900f-88fe-44e9-85e8-c2ac6f011370")
	)
	(text "HSE 8 MHz crystal (MCU-4): PLL /4 x216 /2 = 216 MHz sysclk, /9 = exact 48 MHz USB clock.\nC18/C19 = 2 x (CL 9 pF - 5 pF stray) = 8.2 pF, NP0 only; trim 6.8/10 pF on the bench if the layout runs long.\nRefs chosen 2026-08-15: C1685, 8.2 pF C0G 50 V 0603 (exact computed value). Tolerance C = +/-0.25 pF inferred\nfrom the FH part code; confirm on the datasheet at order time if the AN2867 margin matters.\nLayout: guard ground ring around Y1 and its caps stitched to the MCU VSS, PH0/PH1 loop as short as\npossible, nothing routed under the crystal body."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 216 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "40cb8520-72bd-455a-bef4-2cee25d1222c")
	)
	(text "SWD header (MCU-2 / CON-4): 2.54 mm 1x6 through-hole, mark1 Prog pinout\n1 = 3V3, 2 = SWCLK, 3 = GND, 4 = SWDIO, 5 = NRST, 6 = SWO (PB3).\nNOT assembled: hand-populated with 3 pins (GND, SWCLK, SWDIO); all 6\npositions are routed so the 1:1 cable option stays open. No BOM line.\nSWD nets stay local to this sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 258 100 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5aaab600-d261-4cb1-b2e7-51a021476fad")
	)
	(text "BOOT0 (MCU-3): R3 = 10k pull-down, the pin\nhas no internal pull. JP1 forces BOOT0 high for\nthe system bootloader (DFU recovery path).\nBOOT_ADD1 option byte must never be\nreprogrammed (recovery path)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 168 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5d02a0b2-b5a9-49bc-8cfc-6d92bc4e8d03")
	)
	(text "Not on this sheet: the I2C1 4.7k pull-ups on PB8/PB9 (sensor sheet), the 10k pull-up on\nFLASH_CS/PB12 (storage sheet, the W25Q /CS must track VCC at power-up), the 12 V divider\nand its Schottky feeding 12V_SENSE (power sheet, PWR-4), and the USB 90 ohm pair plus ESD\narray on USB_DM/USB_DP (USB sheet, CON-5, no series resistors).\nPA4 and PA5 are TTa pins (3.3 V max): nothing 5 V may ever touch IMU_CS or SPI1_SCK."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250 216 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a248dfb2-bdc5-4ee0-acf4-c48b0ec256de")
	)
	(text "Free pins left unconnected on purpose (no-connect flags):\nPC13, PC14, PC15 (backup domain, no LSE fitted), PC2, PC3 (spare ADC inputs),\nPA9 (OTG_FS_VBUS - sensing stays disabled, firmware forces B-valid), PA10 (OTG_FS_ID,\ndevice-only board), PA15, PC10, PC11 (UART escape route), PC12.\nThey stay reachable at the package if a respin ever needs them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 140 216 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ad7f9fee-3bee-4aae-84dc-e7e9905b0cef")
	)
	(text "VDDA (pin 13) is tied to +3V3 directly - NO series resistor:\nVDDA is the ADC reference, an IR drop is a reference offset.\nC14 100 nF + C15 1 uF at the pin (DS11853 Figure 28).\nVSSA (pin 12) joins the ground plane at one point near the MCU."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 252 45 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b125dc68-b986-40a9-a29d-9b35bde58709")
	)
	(text "MCU - STM32F722RET6 (MCU-1). Pin assignment per docs/aio-board-pinmap.md"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 30 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b24e16f5-8c7c-4afa-9a36-759ad3effdfa")
	)
	(text "Decoupling per the pin map summary: C8-C11 = one 100 nF per VDD pin (19, 32, 48, 64),\neach placed at its pin on the PCB. C12 = 4.7 uF bulk on 3V3 near the MCU.\nC13 = 100 nF on VBAT (pin 1, tied to +3V3: no coin cell, no RTC backup)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 145 45 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c6e6f17b-5175-4bcd-b751-3b810d15b171")
	)
	(text "VCAP_1 (pin 30): 4.7 uF to VSS. Only VCAP pin on LQFP64, VCAP_2 is absent.\nVCAP_1: plain 4.7uF X5R MLCC fitted (C1779), decided 2026-08-15.\nDS11853 Table 19's 0.1-0.2 ohm ESR window is contradicted by ST's own\npractice: AN4661 calls the same part 'ceramic', every ST board fits plain\nMLCCs (Nucleo-64 MB1136 single-VCAP: 4.7uF ceramic 'ESR<1ohm';\nNucleo-144 MB1137/F722ZE: 2.2uF X7R), and newer families spec ESR as a\nmaximum (H7 <100mR, U5 <20mR). Known deviation from the datasheet letter;\nno field failure ever reported."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104 198 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c9d7cc51-04a4-41f9-91d7-5b9e640ed689")
	)
	(text "NRST (pin 7): 100 nF at the pin (DS11853 Figure 47).\nInternal pull-up 30-50k, no external one.\nNot 5 V tolerant (4.0 V max) - exposed on J1 pin 5."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 90 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d292835a-ac20-4146-a2f0-d5f09569d4b1")
	)
